  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "The two stable but greedy-inactive contextual checkpoints may contain opponent-conditioned sub-argmax logit signal. Across 2,048 balanced states and twelve distinct saved 64-hand contexts per seed, mean contextual logit RMS should exceed 1e-4 and at least 10% of generic residual RMS; if so, a controlled dose increase is informative even if current greedy actions are invariant.",
  "material_change": "Without generating hands or updating weights, hash-verify both frozen checkpoints and raw training evidence, recover each group's final saved context, and query every state under all twelve contexts. Decompose generic versus contextual residual RMS, action disagreement, base-margin crossing slack, and street-seat partitions.",
