  "notes": [
    "This audit selects no checkpoint and touches no policy weights. Its purpose is to distinguish a clear inactive-conditioning mechanism from a sub-argmax signal that may rationally merit geometric dose scaling.",
    "All 49,152 state-context queries were frozen and outcome-blind. The twelve final group contexts per seed were recovered from hash-verified raw learning-hand evidence and were mutually distinct."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Across 2,048 balanced states and twelve saved contexts per checkpoint, contextual logit RMS was nonzero but small: 0.000984/0.000605 versus generic RMS 0.00615/0.00733. Context-to-generic ratios were 16.0% and 8.25%, greedy context disagreement only 0.049% and 0.098%, and margin crossing below 0.2%.",
    "conclusion": "The raw multiplicative architecture learns mostly a generic residual and only weak, non-replicated conditional variation. Blindly scaling its current recipe is not supported. This is a mechanism-level architecture/objective diagnosis, independent of the small run's absolute reward.",
    "decision": "REVISE_CONTEXT_ARCHITECTURE_TO_REMOVE_GENERIC_DOMINANCE",
    "next_step": "Use the admitted calibrated 64-hand classifier as a frozen six-style posterior and train a zero-mean posterior-centered bank of learned policy heads, which structurally forbids a generic residual while retaining exact Standard10 at zero context; rerun a matched two-seed mechanism smoke."
  },
